    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/hd44780.cpp",
     "lines": "699-707",
     "as": "structure"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "key": "0x08..0x0F",
   "name": "Display On/Off Control",
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:HD44780.raw.txt",
     "lines": "1648-1654"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:HD44780.raw.txt",
     "lines": "1780-1790"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/video/hd44780.cpp",
     "lines": "689-698"
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Display on/off control is instruction 0000 1DCB: DB3 is 1 and DB2, DB1 and DB0 carry D, C and B.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:HD44780.raw.txt",
       "lines": "1648-1651",
       "sha": "7a8c3c99f1869b2c16e53b9b14787963aa6156bf67c8b8dffba7f2211adaa823"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Display on/off control stores D, which turns the display on when 1 and off when 0; the display data stays in DDRAM while off.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:HD44780.raw.txt",
       "lines": "1781-1782",
       "sha": "e2fc849224739241bc8d1fc66ee2eb090d3ce84e7ab59baef292a90cc72363b8"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Display on/off control stores C, which shows the cursor when 1 and hides it when 0.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:HD44780.raw.txt",
       "lines": "1783",
       "sha": "daee1bc62452a3ca95e863e3089bd3b5a15fbc2dc39d7249a7ffc5eabc887f1b"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "4",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Even when the cursor disappears, I/D and other specifications do not change during a display data write.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:HD44780.raw.txt",
       "lines": "1783-1784",
       "sha": "05817c49d5520b4208c99a3eb3fee59c51b7659f32946c150e8e520605fb32ab"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "5",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The cursor uses 5 dots in the 8th line for the 5x8 font and in the 11th line for the 5x10 font (Figure 13).",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:HD44780.raw.txt",
       "lines": "1784-1786",
       "sha": "e522720222991786f443e2fa38f8c4c98c39fc4522ad105bbc22b3e6308cdc53"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "6",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Display on/off control stores B, which blinks the character at the cursor when 1.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:HD44780.raw.txt",
       "lines": "1787",
       "sha": "54b0a74ec46cdaf70f91626db55a958eb181304cc6a87a5ee70ecca19f141ae0"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "7",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Blinking switches all blank dots and the displayed characters every 409.6 ms at fcp or fOSC 250 kHz; the cursor and blinking can show together.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:HD44780.raw.txt",
       "lines": "1788-1789",
       "sha": "edfbc6ff0bbf2683b4b413bea4f57cccd529f431020dcbdc91308baaa3e08d19"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "8",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The blink frequency changes with fOSC or fcp: 409.6 x 250/270 = 379.2 ms at 270 kHz.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:HD44780.raw.txt",
       "lines": "1789-1790",
       "sha": "115c5514f0c675b9601e83a8d56bdeb7f9d8ee706c9417df373bf6f761c7c688"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "9",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Table 6 says it sets the entire display (D) on and off, the cursor (C), and blinking of the cursor position character (B).",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:HD44780.raw.txt",
       "lines": "1651-1654",
       "sha": "2ab5ac07d992ad7814790c0c780ed35170d87b88511ff3364ec91677680106a2"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "closed": [
    {
